ose  people aren't gonna reply to you and the  other half well you might get a  half-decent reply when you send that  first email to supply up make sure you  try and establish a good rapport good  rapport is very important because these  people are looking to start a good  business relationship with you just as  much as you are looking to do with them  so in your first email make sure you  include your name wait from and roughly  what you're looking to build  they know a lot more about your business  than you do already and they know what  they can achieve and what they can't if  you tell them that you're looking to do  something way out of the ordinary  chances are they might be able to help  you but there's also a chance they might  not be able to and they will be honest  with you so tell them what you're  looking to do and don't have any  reservations here anybody that tells  them that they want to sign a  nondisclosure agreement or anything like  that straight off the bat they're not  gonna reply to you they're not even  going to be interested so take your time  to try and establish some good rapport  here so this is where it gets a little  bit tricky and experience matters when  you send out a bunch of emails on  Alibaba in regards to a particular  product Alibaba is also going to tell  lots of other suppliers that you've done  so and then they're going to come and  contact you first you haven't talked to  these people you haven't checked out  their resumes and you haven't checked  out their company chances are they're  not that great so make sure you filter  all the emails that come back to you and  make sure you double-check if you've  sent them an email first so this is  where it's that talking samples to the  suppliers and really push the Alibaba  experience as far as they can once  you've been talking to supplier for a  while and establish good rapport they're  going to start trying to convince you to  buy some samples of me and yes at the  beginning you're definitely going to  have to buy some samples nobody's going  to give you free stuff just because  you're looking to start a company and if  they are it's very rare that they're  going to do so when your first sample  arrives this is where you're going to  understand what I'm talking about the  Alibaba experience and the quality of  suppliers on the platform chances are  the supply you've selected doesn't speak  the best English and there's been some  miscommunication in between what you  told them on what they've actually  produced but this is okay this sample  that you've paid for is now a big  investment into the future of your  company what you need to do here is  contact the supplier again and let them  know that there's been an issue tell  them that something's gone wrong and try  and explain what has gone wrong to them  if they're a decent company they're  going to tell you that it's okay and  they're going to try and fix the problem  don't worry about it they'll pay for all  shipping and they'll pay for everything  and they're going to make sure they give  you the best product possible now my  experience this wasn't the case for  those of you don't know I started a  company called wire watches I'll pop a  link in the description for you if you  want to check it out but basically for  me  they sent out a sample that was full of  dust it was full of little particles  behind the glass and I wasn't satisfied  with the quality I sent an email to my  supplier basically asking them for  another strap supplier saying that what  they produced wasn't exactly what I was  looking for and could they help me find  somebody else that we could combined our  forces with and hopefully create one  great product  this was my stepping stone into another  supplier and into another world away  from Alibaba thankfully the company I  was working with at the time was more  than happy to accommodate any of my  concerns and questions so they sent me a  few different emails and I started  chatting to different suppliers outside  of the other bubble platform from here  on in I continued using the same method  to find the suppliers I'm with today now  it took me 11 months to bring my first  watch to market this may seem like a lot  of time and a crazy amount of time to  spend on samples and procurement but I  wasn't willing to spend almost my life  savings at that point in time to start a  company with another company that I had  no trust in this is my only  recommendation to you it took me 11  months to bring my first product to  market this is because it took me a long  time to find a company that spoke good  English and that I could trust this is  the one piece of advice that'll offer to  anybody starting in the econ game in  2019 make sure the company speaks very  good English and make sure you trust  chances are up they've developed five or  six different samples for the same  company you're going to learn to trust  these people and they're going to learn  to trust you once you're happy with the  final sample everything's perfect you're  into place you've first order for your  very first product congratulations  you've just started your first company  from the comfort of your own home if you  have any questions make sure you drop a  comment below and I'll get back to you  as soon as I can  otherwise if you like this video smash  that subscribe button  20-19 style and I'll see you in the next  one
 

